    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.icons\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently `nf-cod-circuit_board` icon is being used to represent an lsp function. And while I personally find that weird - it's easily overridable, so no big deal. The issue is that at a smaller scale this icon looks really similar to just broken icon rendering with a non-nerd font:\n\n<img width=\"25\" height=\"27\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9ae3390-5628-4b35-a368-60e9ca2ce0ec\" />\n<img width=\"25\" height=\"27\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a7ad2b4-5755-4474-9b2b-2f7178ef84f5\" />\n\nI've spent an embarrassing amount of time trying to debug why aerial.nvim isn't rendering icons properly, while in fact it was working perfectly fine. So I'd propose switching to `nf-md-function`:\n\n<img width=\"25\" height=\"27\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb499ffc-aa1c-4ddb-97d0-f731d1d63807\" />",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-27T12:54:47Z",
