    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I kind of agree about the similarity between the \"circuit board\" and \"broken icon rendering\", there is a logic behind using it. All icons in `lsp` category use `nf-cod-*` icons with \"outline\" variant because there are a lot of `nf-cod-sybmol-*` icons present with this look And `nf-md-function` doesn't quite fit in this family, albeit being a better fit.\n\nI remember it was a tough back-and-fourth decision on what is better to use here. As I kind of like how the \"circuit board\" looks and it somewhat fits the theme of \"function\", it was chosen as an alternative for weirdly missing `nf-cod-symbol-function`.\n\nAs \"this looks like not rendered icon\" is a one time confusion (which usually doesn't happen if the terminal emulator and font support \"overflow\" view, [which is suggested](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/946ae64e0ee807ae3c41f382f0114b4ed4915b2c/doc/mini-icons.txt#L42-L48)) and is easily customizable, I think I'll close this as not planned.",
